{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target the Hyperledger Fabric v1.0 architecture (peers, ordering service, channels, chaincode, MSP) as the codebase baseline for all implementation work.",
    "For U3, use the lifecycle system chaincode (LSCC, referred to as LCCC in the story) for chaincode-level upgrades and a system-chaincode-based patching path for non-protocol fixes; protocol upgrades are handled via a versioned peer binary plus a data-format compatibility/migration layer so existing ledger data is preserved.",
    "For U4, migrate all remaining ledger code and ledger tests to the new block structure (common.Block with BlockHeader/BlockData/Envelope payloads) introduced by Gerrit change 2581, and refactor ledger unit tests to use lightweight mock security primitives instead of the real MSP implementation.",
    "For U7, enforce the invocation sanity check in the peer's chaincode support/endorser path: only normal (application) chaincodes or the lifecycle system chaincode may be invoked; any other system chaincode invocation is rejected.",
    "For U2, document the new-channel configuration transaction as a common.Envelope carrying a ConfigEnvelope (channel group hierarchy, mod_policy, values such as Consortium/ChannelCreationPolicy/AnchorPeers, and signatures), aligned with the API from FAB-687 and Gerrit change 1795.",
    "For U8, build the Node SDK in Node.js (JavaScript) using gRPC with protobuf stubs generated from the Fabric protocol definitions; the SDK wraps fabric-ca for enrollment and exposes client/channel/peer/transaction-proposal/query/event APIs.",
    "All documentation (U1, U2, U5, U6) is authored in reStructuredText/Markdown and published through the project's documentation pipeline (ReadTheDocs), with v0.6 content clearly separated and redirected from v1.0 pages.",
    "Unit tests accompany each code activity; integration/system verification and code review are captured as separate cross-cutting activities."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (myself) performs all work; all figures are effort in workdays (1 workday = 8 hours), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "A working Fabric v1.0 development/build environment (Go toolchain, Docker, Gerrit access) and the referenced changes 1795 and 2581 are available.",
    "Node SDK scope (U8) is an initial functional release covering identity enrollment, channel create/join interaction, chaincode install/instantiate/invoke/query, and event listening; full production hardening and advanced features are out of scope for this increment.",
    "U3 covers design plus a reference implementation and test evidence of a protocol-upgrade path with data preservation for the current v1.0 codebase, not a generalized solution for all possible future protocol changes.",
    "U5 deliverables are presentation slides, architecture diagrams/visual aids, and runnable demo scripts describing v1.0 as of approximately sprint 6.",
    "U6 documentation covers the in-development v1.0 usage docs plus clear redirection of users seeking a stable platform to v0.6 docs.",
    "Documentation is produced in English only; no localization effort is included.",
    "Existing continuous integration infrastructure is in place, so only increment-specific CI/test-job adjustments are included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment analysis and solution design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all user stories against the current v1.0 codebase, review referenced Gerrit changes (1795, 2581) and FAB-687, define the overall technical approach, and produce short design notes for the upgrade path, invocation sanity check, and Node SDK scope.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Getting-started/onboarding documentation",
      "activity_description": "Create and restructure quick-start and navigation content so new visitors can get started quickly and find what they need: landing page, prerequisites, install/run first network, and pointers to key topics.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: New-channel configuration transaction documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new-channel configuration transaction produced by the FAB-687 API: structure (Envelope/ConfigEnvelope), all fields, allowed values, policies, and worked examples; reconcile with Gerrit change 1795.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Peer upgrade path design",
      "activity_description": "Design the peer upgrade mechanism for protocol changes without data loss: versioning of data formats, compatibility/migration approach, interaction with LSCC-based chaincode upgrades and SCC-based patching, and rollback considerations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U3: Peer upgrade implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the upgrade support: data-format version markers, ledger/state migration logic executed on peer startup after a protocol change, SCC patch-application path for non-protocol fixes, and operational documentation for performing the upgrade.",
      "most_likely_effort": 15
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U3: Upgrade verification tests",
      "activity_description": "Write and run tests proving upgrade with no data loss: pre-upgrade data creation, upgrade execution, post-upgrade validation of ledger/world state and chaincode operation, plus negative/rollback scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U4: Migrate remaining ledger code to new block structure",
      "activity_description": "Fix the remaining portions of ledger code that still use the old block structure missed by Gerrit change 2581, including transaction construction previously embedded inside ledger tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U4: Refactor ledger tests and remove MSP dependency",
      "activity_description": "Update ledger unit tests to the new block structure and remove their explicit dependency on MSP/security components by introducing mock or stub security primitives.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U5: Architecture presentation, visual aids and demo scripts",
      "activity_description": "Produce slides and architecture diagrams of Fabric v1.0 (as of ~sprint 6) plus runnable demonstration scripts that show current behavior to collaborators and potential customers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U6: v1.0 developer documentation and v0.6 redirection",
      "activity_description": "Maintain up-to-date v1.0 usage documentation reflecting ongoing development, and add clear redirection/labeling so users seeking a stable operational platform are directed to v0.6 documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U7: Chaincode invocation sanity check",
      "activity_description": "Implement validation in the peer chaincode-support/endorser path so that only normal chaincodes or the lifecycle system chaincode can be invoked; add unit and integration tests for allowed and rejected invocations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U8: Node SDK API design",
      "activity_description": "Design the Node.js SDK API surface: client, channel, peer/orderer handles, enrollment via fabric-ca, transaction proposal flow, query, and event subscription; define module structure and generated gRPC/protobuf stubs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U8: Node SDK core implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the SDK: identity enrollment and key storage, channel create/join support, chaincode install/instantiate/invoke/query flows, endorsement proposal assembly and signing, and event hub/event listener integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U8: Node SDK tests and sample application",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for the SDK against a running v1.0 network, and deliver a sample Node.js application demonstrating end-to-end usage (enroll, deploy chaincode, invoke, query, receive events).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration, review and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all work items, run full regression and CI pipelines, address code review feedback via Gerrit, fix defects discovered during system testing, and prepare the increment for delivery.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 106
  }
}
